P-E, the agents' engine's half of spec 001's guard patch: deploy/agents-engine's check_tree_masks (in engine.sh) and
row E7 (in prove-limits.sh) take the bare file-name patterns from .claude/settings.json's read denies (spec 000
contracts/agents-engine.md H8 and E7, as amended on feat/001-cloud-elevation). For the Author's hand only: the folder
is protected (FR-039; .claude/hooks/protected-paths.sh).

Why: P-1 adds three in-tree read denies that are bare file-name patterns, Read(*.tfstate*), Read(*.tfplan), and
Read(*.tfvars*). A pattern like that can match in any folder, so no line of tree-masks.txt can hold it, and
check_tree_masks refused to start the engine while the settings named one: its step 1 let only the .env globs
through. The Author's decision, 2026-11-10: "Derive from settings (Recommended)".

Built on 2026-11-10 from plain copies (a `git archive` of feat/001-cloud-elevation at 8b4fd0f1, an edited copy beside
it, `diff -u`), never `git apply` or a write into a worktree. Apply it from the repository's top with `patch -p1`,
which skips this preamble, after P-1, on feat/001-cloud-elevation-p.

  - engine.sh: bare_name_glob; check_tree_masks's step 1 lets each deny with no / and a glob character through, but
    an env glob, which step 3 holds as before; a new step 4 walks the tree once for them all and refuses while a
    file one matches sits outside a mask, naming the pattern and the file. A later *.pem or *.key in the settings
    needs no engine patch.
  - prove-limits.sh, row E7: deny_name_glob takes the same patterns from the settings; the in-container walk
    reports a file one matches (the patterns after --); and engine.sh up runs once with a planted file for each
    pattern glob_sample can name (a leading * made __h4-prove-e7), and must refuse, naming it.
  - test/test_engine_sh.py and test/test_prove_limits_sh.py: their tests, RED before the code on a patched export
    (the combined note, Verification).

